WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.840
You shovel soil onto your flat roof to grow a garden.

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:07.410
And one storm later, there are tons of wet muds sitting above your bed.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:14.320
So the soil comes off and you spread a thin layer of baked clay pebbles that stays light even when it's soaked.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:19.670
You plant grass, but that thin layer dries out fast and the lawn turns brown.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.430
So you switch to see them.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.720
Tiny succulents that keep water in their fat leaves.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:30.610
Next spring, the ceiling starts dripping because the roots crept into a seam in the roof looking for water.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.600
Everything comes up again and down goes a rubber sheet that roots can't get through.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.160
Then a summer storm floods the roof.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.520
The water can't drain and the seeedum starts to rot.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:45.360
So under the pebbles goes a plastic sheet shaped like an egg cartton.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.560
Whose cups hold a little rain and let the rest drain away.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.550
Now, the bedroom below stays cooler all summer and your roof is a garden that waters itself.
